0,Atakapa language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atakapa_language,"In 1919 John R. Swanton proposed a Tunican language family that would include Atakapa, Tunica, and Chitimacha; Morris Swadesh would later provide work focusing on connections between Atakapa and Chitimacha.",Atakapa,Language isolate
1,Atakapa - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atakapa,"They included several distinct bands. They spoke the Atakapa language, which was a linguistic isolate. After 1762, when Louisiana was transferred to Spain following French defeat in the Seven Years' War, little was written about the Atakapa as a people.",Atakapa,Language isolate
